NAME
        bal asyncapi - Generate a Ballerina listener or client from an AsyncAPI contract,
                       or generate an AsyncAPI specification from a Ballerina service file.

SYNOPSIS
        bal asyncapi <input> --protocol <http|ws> [-o <dir>] [--module <name>] [--license <file>]
                     [--with-tests] [--service <name>] [--format <yaml|json>]

DESCRIPTION
        Generate Ballerina sources from the given AsyncAPI definition (.yaml, .yml or .json),
        or generate an AsyncAPI specification from a Ballerina service file (.bal).
        The direction is taken from the input: a definition generates code, a .bal file
        generates a definition.

        Options a protocol does not support are reported as warnings and ignored.

OPTIONS
        <input>
                Path to the AsyncAPI definition or the Ballerina source file.

        --protocol <http|ws>
                Protocol of the AsyncAPI definition. Required.

        -o, --output <dir>
                Directory the generated files are written to. Defaults to the current directory.

        --module <name>
                Module of the Ballerina package the generated files are written to.

        --license <file>
                File with the license header placed on generated files (ws only).

        --with-tests
                Generate test files along with the code (ws only).

        --service <name>
                Service to generate the AsyncAPI definition for (Ballerina source input only).

        --json
                Write the generated AsyncAPI definition as JSON (Ballerina source input only).

        -h, --help
                Display this help.

EXAMPLES
        Generate a WebSocket client with tests.
            $ bal asyncapi chat.yaml --protocol ws --with-tests

        Generate an HTTP webhook listener into a module.
            $ bal asyncapi events.yaml --protocol http --module events -o ./pkg

        Generate an AsyncAPI definition from a Ballerina service.
            $ bal asyncapi service.bal --protocol ws --service chat --json
